WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.604
Picture it: a cruise with the whole family.

2
00:00:03.604 --> 00:00:09.036
The kids are at the pool, grandma's at the buffet — and your text?

3
00:00:09.036 --> 00:00:10.200
Not going anywhere.

4
00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:12.140
There's no signal at sea.

5
00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:18.431
On the cruise where CruiseMesh was born, ship messaging cost seven dollars per phone, per day.

6
00:00:18.431 --> 00:00:26.970
For a family of four, that's nearly two hundred dollars in a week — just to say "meet at the buffet at six."

7
00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:28.705
CruiseMesh is different.

8
00:00:28.705 --> 00:00:38.400
Text your family when there's no signal — free on board, end-to-end encrypted, no accounts, no SIM card, no internet package.

9
00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:40.510
It uses whatever's around.

10
00:00:40.510 --> 00:00:45.350
Phones find each other over the ship's Wi-Fi, no internet needed.

11
00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:47.990
Up close, they talk over Bluetooth.

12
00:00:47.990 --> 00:00:52.390
And family phones carry sealed messages along, until paths cross.

13
00:00:52.740 --> 00:01:02.614
And when any one phone does get online — with an optional pass, or your own server — it carries the whole family's messages home and back.

14
00:01:02.614 --> 00:01:05.540
Sealed envelopes, that no one else can read.

15
00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:08.914
Messages that find a way through.

16
00:01:08.914 --> 00:01:09.418
CruiseMesh.

17
00:01:09.418 --> 00:01:13.450
Free and open source, at cruisemesh dot app.
